Many of the exceptions are rare, so here's what I conclude:

Early in the dungeon you tend to encounter weak monsters that are
worth zero.  Stay shallow and your alignment stays low.  When you
go deep you tend to encounter strong monsters that are worth at
least 5.  Go deep and your alignment quickly hits max.

To me this means that early on killing peacefulls is very bad but
later on it no longer matters.  Using the table will tell you
when.  In particular the mines are filled with monsters peacefull
to gnomes so a gnomish player will have to leave many sources of
armour in the mines and come back later.


